      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          Can I order sustainable or organic pet clothing with certification?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>Yes. GOTS certification covers organic cotton from fibre to finished garment. GRS covers recycled polyester fill and outer fabric. BCI covers Better Cotton sourcing. Every sustainability claim is backed by a named, auditable certification | not a self-declared eco-friendly label.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          How do I get started with a custom pet clothing manufacturer?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>The easiest start is submitting a sample request with your design idea, target animal, size range, and preferred fabric. The production team responds within one business day with a quote and timeline. No bulk commitment is required at the sample stage. Start here | <a href="/tools/sample-request" style="color: var(--color-accent);">/sample-request/</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="section-lowmoq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__header">
      <span class="section__label">Low MOQ Production</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">How 300 Pieces Actually Splits Across Sizes and Colours</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="text-content">
      <p>The 300-piece minimum applies per style, not per size or colour. In practice that gives you a few ways to structure a first order:</p>
      
      <ul class="product-list">
        <li class="product-list__item">One colourway across a full size run | for example 30 XS, 70 S, 100 M, 70 L, 30 XL for a dog hoodie</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Two colourways of the same pattern split evenly | 150 units each in black and red, same size curve</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">A narrower size range with deeper quantities | useful if your target breed mix sits mostly in 2-3 sizes rather than the full curve</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">What counts as a separate style, and needs its own 300-piece minimum: a different fabric, a different pattern or cut, or a meaningfully different construction (a lined coat versus an unlined one, for example). What doesn't reset the count: different colours of the identical pattern, or splitting one design across your full size curve.</p>
      
      <p>If you're not sure how your specific product breaks down, send us the design and we'll tell you directly whether it's one style or several before you commit to quantities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

